SOURCE-AVAILABLE, NOT OPEN SOURCE
=================================

This repository is readable. That is not the same as being free to use, and this file exists
because the absence of one is ambiguous: a repository with no licence is already "all rights
reserved" by default under copyright law, but silence reads as an oversight rather than as a
decision. It is a decision.

No permission is granted to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, sell, or
create derivative works from any part of this repository, except as set out below.

In particular, and without limiting the above: you may not compile and distribute this game or any
part of it, publish it to any storefront or hosting service, or incorporate its code, data,
artwork, audio or design into another work.


WHAT YOU MAY DO
===============

1. READ IT. Anything published here is published deliberately.

2. FORK IT ON GITHUB. Making a repository public on GitHub grants every GitHub user the right to
   view and fork it under GitHub's Terms of Service, and that grant is not withdrawn here. It
   extends to forking within GitHub and to nothing further.

3. ASK. Permission for anything else is available and may well be given. Contact
   scrapyard@panimu.com and say what you want to do.


THIRD-PARTY CONTENT, WHICH THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER
======================================================

Nothing above claims rights over work that is not mine. Two categories:

VENDORED ARTWORK, in `assets/`
    Every pack in that directory is public domain (CC0 1.0 Universal) and is vendored whole and
    unmodified, from Kenney, Dungeon Crawl Stone Soup, Pixel Frog and Quaternius. It is CC0 whether
    or not it sits in this repository, and my copyright does not attach to it. Each source
    directory carries its own README naming the exact upstream page, the exact file and the date;
    `assets/README.md` indexes them. If you want that art, take it from its source, where it is
    free and where you will get the whole pack.

    The sprites in `public/sprites/` are generated FROM those packs by the build tools in `tools/`.
    They are derivative works of public-domain material, which places no obligation on you, but the
    composition, palette and arrangement are mine and are covered by this licence.

DEPENDENCIES
    Everything installed by `npm` or NuGet - PixiJS, MonoGame and the rest - is governed by its own
    licence and is not redistributed here.


